---
import DocLayout from '../../layouts/DocLayout.astro';
import MainPanelTabs from '../../components/MainPanelTabs.astro';
---

<DocLayout title="Light Properties">
  <h1>Main Panel — Light Properties</h1>
  <MainPanelTabs activeTab="main-panel/light-properties" />
  <p>
    The <strong>Light Properties</strong> section within the Main Panel UI mirrors and expands Blender's native light data blocks. It exposes immediate adjustments for individual emitters.
  </p>

  <hr class="my-8 border-white/5" />

  <h2>── 1. Exposure and Color Management ──</h2>
  <p>
    Quickly tweak essential parameters from the central list item:
  </p>
  <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-xs mb-6">
    <li><strong>Exposure Slider:</strong> Calibrate energy output in Watts or custom exposure values.</li>
    <li><strong>Color Temperature (Kelvin):</strong> Slide between warm tungsten (2000K) and cold skylight (10000K) with visual color feedback.</li>
    <li><strong>Texture Emitter Mapping:</strong> Load high-fidelity softbox HDR textures directly onto Cycles Emitter Nodes.</li>
  </ul>

  <hr class="my-8 border-white/5" />

  <h2>── 2. Emitter Isolation ──</h2>
  <p>
    Isolate light contributions instantly. Toggling a light's "Solo" button locks out the rest of the scene, allowing you to examine specular highlights and direct illumination paths in isolation.
  </p>
</DocLayout>
